      "message": "Yes, I understand the idea behind this: auto-ack is a broker/subscriber configuration, not something that changes message by message.\n\nThat said, I think moving `isAutoAck()` from `MessageAcknowledgement` to `BrokerApi` makes the consumer API harder to use.\n\nThe decision of whether to call ack() is needed by the client while it is processing a message. At that point, the consumer callback only has two things: the event and the acknowledgement handle. It does not have the `BrokerApi`.\n\nSo consumers (like multi-site) would no longer be able to decide locally whether to call `ack()` unless we also inject/pass the broker API, or pass the auto-ack flag separately.\n\nLet\u0027s discuss this",
